<title>SOUTH AFRICA: CRICKET-AUSTRALIA BEAT BORDER BY AN INNINGS AND 105 RUNS.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-AUSTRALIA BEAT BORDER BY AN INNINGS AND 105 RUNS.</headline>
<dateline>EAST LONDON 1997-03-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia beat Border by an</p>
<p>innings and 105 runs on the second day of their three day match</p>
<p>at Buffalo Park on Saturday.</p>
<p>Scores:</p>
<p>Border 117 (Jason Gillespie 7-34) and 148 (Pieter Strydom</p>
<p>55)</p>
<p>Australia 370-9 declared (Greg Blewett 112, Mark Waugh 62)</p>
</text>
